version: "1.0"

metadata:
  title: "Deriving the Speed of Light in a Vacuum"
  author: "MathTS Workbook"
  description: "A live, self-verifying derivation of c via Maxwell's relation and a wavelength-frequency cross-check, with rendered equations and a chart — all MathTS-native."
  tags: [physics, electromagnetism, constants, derivation]

runtime:
  engine: mathts
  execution: reactive

cells:
  - markdown: |
      # Deriving the Speed of Light in a Vacuum

      The speed of light **c** follows from two electromagnetic constants of
      free space — the vacuum permittivity **ε₀** and the vacuum permeability
      **μ₀** — via Maxwell's relation:
    id: intro

  - equation: "c = 1 / sqrt(epsilon_0 * mu_0)"
    id: maxwellEq

  - markdown: |
      ## 1. Maxwell's relation

      ε₀ and μ₀ in SI units (MathTS's `electricConstant` and `magneticConstant`):
    id: maxwellIntro

  - code: "8.8541878128e-12"
    id: eps0

  - code: "1.25663706212e-6"
    id: mu0

  - code: "1 / sqrt(eps0 * mu0)"
    id: cMaxwell
    depends_on: [eps0, mu0]

  - code: "299792458"
    id: cDefined

  - test: "abs(cMaxwell - cDefined) / cDefined < 1e-6"
    id: checkMaxwell
    depends_on: [cMaxwell, cDefined]

  - markdown: |
      ## 2. Wavelength–frequency cross-check

      In vacuum, every wave satisfies c = λ·ν:
    id: lambdaNuIntro

  - equation: "c = lambda * nu"
    id: lambdaNuEq

  - markdown: |
      A HeNe laser line: λ ≈ 632.8 nm, ν ≈ 4.738×10¹⁴ Hz.
    id: heneNote

  - code: "632.8e-9"
    id: lambda

  - code: "4.738e14"
    id: nu

  - code: "lambda * nu"
    id: cLambdaNu
    depends_on: [lambda, nu]

  - test: "abs(cLambdaNu - cDefined) / cDefined < 0.01"
    id: checkLambdaNu
    depends_on: [cLambdaNu, cDefined]

  - markdown: |
      ## 3. Dispersion-free vacuum

      Across the visible spectrum, frequency is exactly inverse to wavelength
      (ν = c/λ), since c is constant:
    id: chartIntro

  - data: "[4.0e-7, 5.0e-7, 6.0e-7, 7.0e-7]"
    id: lambdas

  - code: "cDefined ./ lambdas"
    id: nus
    depends_on: [cDefined, lambdas]

  - visualization: |
      type: line
      title: "Vacuum: frequency vs wavelength (ν = c/λ)"
      x: { label: "wavelength λ (m)", data: lambdas }
      y: { label: "frequency ν (Hz)", data: nus }
    id: dispersionChart
    depends_on: [lambdas, nus]

  - markdown: |
      ## Conclusion

      Both routes reproduce **c = 299,792,458 m/s** — Maxwell's relation to
      floating-point precision and λ·ν to measurement tolerance — and the green
      `test` cells make the document self-verifying.
    id: conclusion
